  "command": "node scripts/bench/measure-server-boot.mjs --launches=3 --out=work/server-boot.json",
  "method": [
    "scripts/speed/stack.mjs is absent. The retained benchmark launches the real Next dev CLI, separately bundled WS entry, and separately tsx-loaded WS entry.",
    "Each launch uses an isolated data directory and fixture git repository. WS has no Next sibling, exposing the previous ten-second readiness timeout.",
    "Health means a complete HTTP 200 JSON response identifying product o8, not the Ready console line.",
    "Compiled WS uses the packaged esbuild bundle format, native externals and server-only stub. Compilation time is excluded from process bootstrap.",
    "Next framework trace spans overlap and must not be summed. The original compile-path sequence covers instrumentation twice, middleware, then panel/status.",
    "Normal persisted Next dev and tsx caches are retained between launches. OS cache is uncontrolled; these are repeated process boots, not an empty compiler-cache guarantee.",
    "An earlier after-change Next cohort took 4459, 4332 and 4445 ms. The final idle cohort below meets three seconds with the normal persisted dev cache; the clean compiler-cache target remains unproven.",
    "Initial diagnostic instrumentation was collected before implementation. Its Next times are cumulative process milliseconds; WS times are per-phase durations. The initial 500 ms probe timeout differs from the retained benchmark's uninterrupted 20 s timeout, so its totals are not the comparison cohort.",
    "Raw application logs, local filesystem identities, and credentials are excluded."
  ],
